This is an iterative self-review pass for verb and noun displacement, not ordinary conversation.

Privately review all five current writings. Create replacements only where you see a meaningful improvement.

For each replacement:
- use the exact candidate id;
- treat newWordSet as exactly [noun, displacedVerb];
- you may switch the noun, the displaced verb, or both;
- the noun and verb should still create an unexpected displacement rather than an ordinary default action;
- the proposed displaced verb must not duplicate the displaced verb of any other current candidate;
- rewrite the completion so the whole piece is beautiful, deep, funny, interesting, exciting, or otherwise stronger;
- explicitly use both returned words;
- the supplied seedWords array contains nouns only; you may use it for a fresh noun idea, not as a verb list;
- keep it concise and recognizably yours;
- score the old and new versions from 0 to 100 using the same standard.

The runtime keeps the version with the higher score. A tie keeps the old version.

Return only a JSON array. Each item must contain exactly:
- id
- oldScore
- newWordSet
- newWriting
- newScore

Omit unchanged candidates. Return [] when you propose no replacements. Do not return explanations, markdown, or extra fields.
